<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements of OpenArcCore.framework/Versions/A/Helpers/openarc_helper, the child-process
  executable of the Chromium engine (plan C8), used by scripts/make-app.sh (ad-hoc signing,
  hardened runtime).

  One executable runs every child process type until plan C10 splits it into helper apps
  (renderer, GPU, plugin, alerts) with one entitlements file each, as Chrome does. Until then it
  carries the minimum the hardened runtime needs for all of them:
  - com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit: V8 (renderer, utility) and the GPU process map JIT code
    (MAP_JIT). Chrome's renderer and GPU helpers carry exactly this key.
  - com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation: the helper dlopen()s the framework's
    library (../OpenArcCore). Ad-hoc signatures carry no Team ID, so library validation would
    refuse it, as it does Sparkle in the app (OpenArc.entitlements). Remove once D6 signs
    everything with one Developer ID team.
  No App Sandbox: the helpers use Chromium's own seatbelt sandbox.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key>
  <true/>
  <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
